## New findings

| # | Severity | File:Lines | Issue |
|---|----------|------------|-------|
| N1 | HIGH | `store.rs:1059 vs 1079-1080` | `clear_for_replace` runs *before* canonical in-store re-check. Differ dest via symlinked-parent/`..` into store is deleted, then refused. Direct in-store path is safe (lexical fence `:1043` fires first), so test `:1807` passes but guarantee "refusal leaves store untouched" fails for canonical paths. Fix: move clear after `:1080` check. |
| N2 | MEDIUM | `store.rs:534-560` | `Same` path hashes then chmods with no re-verify; swap in between returns `AlreadyPresent` with wrong bytes. Contradicts "every loss is a loud refusal, never silent corruption" (`:975`). |
| N3 | MEDIUM | `store.rs:836` (`write`) | "Already present and verified" comment is false: `contains()` (`is_file`) trusts presence without hashing. Corrupt entry makes `write` a no-op; later `read` fails. Pre-existing, adjacent to this change. |
| N4 | MEDIUM | tests | Gaps: no corrupt-store+Differ-preservation test (the core verify-before-clear property); no canonical-in-store+Differ test (would catch N1); bare-name e2e `:1955` is `#[ignore]` so never runs in CI; symlink arms `:2010,:2064` compile out on Windows ÔÇö the platform run here. |
| N5 | LOW | `store.rs:588-625,264` | `clear`/`make_readonly` statÔåÆchmodÔåÆremove on paths: swap after check chmods victim through symlink. Disclosed in residual-race note, but `clear`'s "swap is refused" (`:1055`) overclaims intra-call window. |
| N6 | LOW | `store.rs:1090` | Sweep deletes any matching tmp in dir, so concurrent same-dir different-artifact installs can delete a live peer tmp (linkÔåÆrename window). Doc says only "same-dest" unsupported; scope is same-dir. Plus per-file full dir scan = O(N┬▓) for big installs. |
| N7 | LOW | docs | Overclaims: "refused materialization leaves no destination behind" (`:940`) false when Differ+corrupt-store preserves dest; checklist counts "4 more tests" then lists 5; evidence date `2026-10-30` vs today `10-29`; stale allow-comment `:1307` names `settle_destination` instead of `clear_for_replace`. |

Suggested next: fix N1 ordering, re-verify N2 wording, add the two Differ-preservation tests + un-ignore bare-name (serial) or gate it, then re-run `cargo test -p qqq-pkg` + clippy.

